  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OGB Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The responses in Lebanon aims to address the needs of people affected by the escalation of violence in the region. Humanitarian efforts will provide support to people in need through a multi-sectoral approach, including e.g. access to clean drinking water, hot meals, and hygiene kits. Most of the affected people are displaced internally.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Lebanon</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam has been working in Lebanon since 2006; it has a regional Gender Justice Hub that administers a regional gender justice programme and a Lebanon programme that focuses on three thematic areas of work: Humanitarian, Economic Justice, and Active Citizenship &lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;)&gt; Governance. Over the course of the past three years, Oxfam in Lebanon has integrated its humanitarian and development programming into a #one programme approach#, as described in the Oxfam Country Strategy. The humanitarian component of the strategy looks at the continuation of life-saving WaSH service provision, protection services and cash assistance, while in parallel the development programs, in collaboration with local authorities and civil society, aim to address the underlying root causes of inequality and poverty over the longer-term, including through policy change.
Our vision is that, by the end of 2021, marginalized women and men (Lebanese, Palestinian and Syrian populations including refugees)are protected and empowered to enjoy their basic rights, enabling them to live in dignity within a more equitable society.
Oxfam inLebanon has a main office in Beirut, and two operational offices in Zahle (Bekaa governance) and Tripoli (North governance).</narrative>
  </participating-org>
